            "content": [
              {
                "type": "ministry",
                "heading": "MINISTRY OF WORKS & HOUSING"
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "1",
                "text": "Property of the Union (not being railway, naval, military or air force works or being the property of the Department of Atomic Energy) except (1) buildings, the construction of which has been financed otherwise than from the civil works budget and (ii) buildings, the control of which has at the time of construction or subsequently been permanently made over by the Ministry of Works & Housing to another Ministry."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "2",
                "text": "All Government Civil works and buildings including those of Union Territorles excluding roads and excluding works executed by or buildings belonging to the Railways and the Department of Atomic Energy."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "3",
                "text": "Horticultural operations."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "4",
                "text": "Indian Service of Engineers."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "5",
                "text": "Development of Government colonies in Delhi"
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "6",
                "text": "Allotment of Government lands in Delhi"
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "7",
                "text": "Administration of Government estates under the control of the Ministry of Works & Housing at Delhi, Bombay, Calcutta, Simla, Nagpur, etc. Move of offices outside Delhi including the satellite townships around Delhi; deconcentration of offices from Bombay and Calcutta; location of new offices in Delhi, Calcutta, Bombay and Simla"
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "8",
                "text": "Aliotment of accommodation in Vigyan Bhavan."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "9",
                "text": "Administration of the Requisitioning and Acquisition of Immovable Property Act, 1952."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "10",
                "text": "Control and administration of Hotel Janpath, New Delhi, Grand Hotel Simla and Government Hostels."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "11",
                "text": "Administration of Delhi Hotels (Control of Accommodation) Act. 1949."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "12",
                "text": "The Public Premises (Eviction of Unauthorised Occupants) Act, 1958."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "13",
                "text": "Administration of Rehabilitation Markets-Raisina Road Market; Sarojini Market, Sarojini Nagar; New Central Market, Connaught Circus Kamla Market and Pleasure Garden Market."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "14",
                "text": "Formulation of housing policy and programme. Review of the implementation of the Plan Schemes. Collection and dissemination of data on housing, building materials and building techniques. General measures for reduction of building costs. International cooperation and technical assistance in housing."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "15",
                "text": "Stationery and printing for the Government of India including official publications."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "16",
                "text": "Administration of the Indian Boilers Act and the Regulations made thereunder; Central Boilers Board."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "17",
                "text": "Explosives, administration of the Indian Explosives Act, 1884, the Petroleum Act, 1934, and the Rules made thereunder; but not the Explosive Substances Act."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "18",
                "text": "The Ashoka Hotels Ltd., New Delhi."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "19",
                "text": "All Attached or Subordinate Offices or other organisations concerned with any of the subjects specified in this list."
              },
              {
                "type": "entry",
                "num": "20",
                "text": "Public sector projects falling under the subjects included in this list except such projects as are specifically allotted to any other Department."
              }
            ],
